; Import library for the Vulkan loader.
;
; There is no Vulkan SDK on this machine, so vulkan-1.lib does not exist and
; `zig build -lvulkan-1` cannot resolve it. The loader DLL itself is present in
; System32 (vulkaninfo works), so the import library is generated from a
; definition file that names the loader and the four entry points this project
; calls directly.
;
; Generated once with:
;   zig dlltool -d vulkan-1.def -l vulkan-1.lib -D vulkan-1.dll
;
; Only the commands the probe uses are listed. Everything else is reached
; through vkGetInstanceProcAddr / vkGetDeviceProcAddr at runtime, which is how a
; real Vulkan application does it anyway.
;
; vkGetDeviceProcAddr is here for a specific reason. This loader returns NULL for
; `vkGetInstanceProcAddr(NULL, "vkGetDeviceProcAddr")`, which the spec requires
; it to return, so a probe that discovers the device resolver dynamically never
; gets one. Linking it directly sidesteps that and matches how an application
; that links vulkan-1 behaves.

LIBRARY vulkan-1
EXPORTS
    vkEnumerateInstanceVersion
    vkEnumerateInstanceExtensionProperties
    vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties
    vkCreateInstance
    vkGetInstanceProcAddr
    vkGetDeviceProcAddr
